		{
			"identifier": "MaryOBlock",
			"uid": 106884,
			"tags": [],
			"exportToToc": false,
			"allowOutOfBounds": true,
			"doc": "One of Mary-O's REACTIVE blocks — the ones that answer a head-bonk from below.  What it LOOKS like and what it HOLDS are separate fields, on purpose: a block that looks like a brick but really has a powerup is a thing you should be able to author.  `kind` — what it looks like:    Question  a ?-block. Wears its own texture, and an inert one once spent.   Quasar    the pocket-quasar block, which wears its own texture too.   Brick     masonry. Breakable ONLY when it holds nothing — a loaded brick behaves like a ?-block wearing brick art, which is the classic behaviour.  `contents` — what it holds. Leave it BLANK for the sensible default for that look (a Question levels toward the lantern, a Quasar always gives a quasar, a Brick holds nothing), or say:    Empty           nothing. A Brick that holds nothing is the one that breaks.   AlwaysWand      always the star wand, whatever form she is in.   AlwaysLantern   always the cinder beacon.   AlwaysQuasar    always a pocket quasar.   TowardWand      the next rung on the way to the wand.   TowardLantern   the next rung on the way to the lantern — small gets the wand, tall gets the lantern. This is what every ?-block in 1-1 does.  One tile, floating at bonk height over ground she can stand on. The block's collision and art come from this entity; nothing else has to be authored for it to work.  An unknown kind or an unknown contents is REFUSED at load rather than becoming a plain wall — a block that silently stopped being special still stops the player, so the level would look whole with one bonus quietly gone.",
			"tileOpacity": 1.0,
			"lineOpacity": 1.0,
			"fillOpacity": 0.08,
			"hollow": false,
			"color": "#E8A33D",
			"renderMode": "Tile",
			"showName": true,
			"tilesetId": 106934,
